2026-05-09  "new map" button + seed display
  WHAT: Top-right button regenerates the world with a fresh
        random seed. Old layers .destroy()ed so Pixi releases
        their GPU buffers; new layers built and added; camera
        recentered + zoom reset. Readout grew a third line
        showing the current seed (so a map you like is
        identifiable). main.ts factored: world/layers now
        mutable, addLayers() + loadMap() helpers.
  WHY:  User asked. Default seed (1337) was hardcoded for
        reproducibility during nail-to-nail dev (so "nation
        #14 with 4 borders" stays the same across reloads),
        but it made worldgen feel broken. Button preserves
        the reproducibility default while letting the user
        sample variety. Seed in readout means a good map can
        be remembered. Future: if reproducibility matters
        more, we'll add a ?seed= URL param too.

