2026-05-09  Nail #4: region adjacency graph (data only)
  WHAT: Region now carries `neighbors: number[]` — sorted unique
        list of region ids sharing a tile-edge (4-way, edge-only;
        diagonals don't count, water gaps don't count). Built in
        a single O(N) sweep at the end of generateWorld: for
        each tile check the +x and +y neighbor; if both are
        land and differ, add each to the other's set. Sets are
        flattened to sorted arrays before storing on Region.
        Readout extended: "borders N" appended to the player-
        nation line as a smoke test that the data is real.
  WHY:  Adjacency is the prerequisite for everything multi-
        region: army moves cap to neighbors, vassal/diplomacy
        graph lookups, neighbor-aware AI, threat assessment.
        Pure data work today; no visual. Edge-only chosen over
        8-way because it matches the boundary lines we already
        draw and avoids "your region touches that other one
        because of a single corner pixel" false positives.
        Coastal/naval adjacency deferred — comes when we have
        ships.

