2026-05-09  Nail #3: player nation + zoom cap + tier relabel
  WHAT: Three changes wiring up the operational tier from the
        new 3-tier view model:
        1. world.ts gen now picks `playerRegionId` =
           argmax(tileCount). Largest region = your home base.
           Stable across reloads because seed is fixed.
        2. mapRender.ts: tint alpha forks (player 0.55, others
           0.28) so your territory pops at any zoom; new
           playerLayer Graphics traces a thicker WHITE outline
           (3px, alpha 0.95) along just the player region's
           border. Stacks on top of the standard dark borders.
        3. main.ts: maxZoom dropped 8 → 2.0 (manual pinch can no
           longer reach the old crossfade-out point). Tier label
           computed from cellPixelSize: ≤18 → STRATEGIC,
           >18 → OPERATIONAL. The MID + crossfade-percent
           machinery is gone; tints/borders no longer fade with
           zoom. TACTICAL stays in the type for future battle-
           snap usage but is unreachable from manual zoom.
        4. store.ts: ViewLabel = STRATEGIC | OPERATIONAL |
           TACTICAL (was STRATEGIC | MID | TACTICAL).
        Readout now: "zoom Xx — STRATEGIC/OPERATIONAL — your
        nation: region #N".
  WHY:  Per the new Pillar #6: manual zoom should never reveal
        soldiers; that's tactical, reserved for battle. Capping
        zoom + relabeling makes the tier model legible. Player
        concept introduced now because "operational view = your
        nation in detail" requires there BE a your-nation. White
        outline + dim-others is the smallest visual move that
        distinguishes you without committing to a final UI
        treatment. Bundle: ~74 KB gz main entry, ~220 KB total.

