2026-05-09  port.md: 3-tier view + future-scope un-cut + open Qs
  WHAT: Three structural updates to port.md after the user
        proposed a refined view model and confirmed long-term
        building/settlement scope:
        1. Pillar #6 rewritten as "Three-tier view, one
           simulation":
             • Strategic (zoomed out)
             • Operational (zoomed in, manual cap) — your
               nation in detail, armies as formation icons.
               Manual pinch caps here. No individual soldiers.
             • Tactical (battle only) — pixel-art sprite-and-
               formation view; entered ONLY via attack order
               (auto-snap) or tap on a battle-in-progress badge.
        2. Hard cuts split into two sections:
             • Hard cuts (forever): decrees, commander tree,
               masteries, doctrine, vassal-as-region,
               ARMY_MODE flag, diplomacy menu system.
             • Deferred scope (long-term v2, NOT now): barracks,
               airstrips, warship factory, energy factory,
               markets, houses, mines, plus ships, planes,
               multi-resource, ground ops, bombs/nukes, trade
               markets. Frozen until the core loop is fun
               (lesson #4 cited explicitly as the guardrail).
        3. Open questions section: sea travel & island
           handling, with default = bias gen toward one
           connected continent until ships are un-deferred.
  WHY:  User: "How about this behavior: allow the zoom in but
        don't directly go into the full tactical zoom yet. I
        should see all of my nations land and settlements and
        building / armies. If I send army into battle, the view
        should go to that full tactical view then." Plus
        confirmed full building list is the long-term vision
        ("but not there yet"). Captured BEFORE any code so the
        new model has a single authoritative reference and the
        un-cut scope is visibly fenced behind the "core loop
        first" guardrail. Nail #3 candidates discussed next.

